<MiscSettings xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">

  <ResolutionOptions>
    <ResolutionOption>
      <Width>1024</Width>
      <Height>720</Height>
    </ResolutionOption>
    <ResolutionOption>
      <Width>1280</Width>
      <Height>720</Height>
    </ResolutionOption>
    <ResolutionOption>
      <Width>1366</Width>
      <Height>768</Height>
    </ResolutionOption>
    <ResolutionOption>
      <Width>1440</Width>
      <Height>900</Height>
    </ResolutionOption>
    <ResolutionOption>
      <Width>1600</Width>
      <Height>900</Height>
    </ResolutionOption>
    <ResolutionOption>
      <Width>1680</Width>
      <Height>1050</Height>
    </ResolutionOption>
    <ResolutionOption>
      <Width>1920</Width>
      <Height>1080</Height>
    </ResolutionOption>
    <ResolutionOption>
      <Width>1920</Width>
      <Height>1200</Height>
    </ResolutionOption>
    <ResolutionOption>
      <Width>2560</Width>
      <Height>1440</Height>
    </ResolutionOption>
    <ResolutionOption>
      <Width>3840</Width>
      <Height>2160</Height>
    </ResolutionOption>
  </ResolutionOptions>
  
  <AllLevelTips>
    <LevelTips>
      <Levelname>Forest-grove</Levelname>
      <Tips>
        <string>Place traps like Bearjaws and then lure enemies into them.</string>
      </Tips>
    </LevelTips>
    <LevelTips>
      <Levelname>Apollo-upperpalace</Levelname>
      <Tips>
        <string>Use the Drop of Radiance potion to easily light dark areas.</string>
      </Tips>
    </LevelTips>
    <LevelTips>
      <Levelname>Ares</Levelname>
      <IsTriggered>DiomedesDead</IsTriggered>
      <Tips>
        <string>Use the Altar of Zephar in difficult areas to leave an area and come back stronger</string>
      </Tips>
    </LevelTips>
  </AllLevelTips>

  <Tips>
    <string>Use the altar of Zephyr to quickly travel throughout Mount Olympus.</string>
    <string>Hit an opponent in the head, and they will be more severely wounded.</string>
    <string>Hit an opponent in the legs, and they will be knocked down.</string>
    <string>Watch the green stamina bar or your attack speed will slow down.</string>
    <string>Overhead attacks are slightly slower, but land head-strikes more easily.</string>
    <string>Thrust attacks are fast, and have longer reach.</string>
    <string>Uppercut attacks are good for knocking opponents off their feet.</string>
    <string>Successfully blocking with a shield will leave the enemy dazed. Quickly counter-attack!</string>
    <string>Lamps and torches will splash burning oil when they are broken.</string>
    <string>Time your attacks carefully. Mashing buttons will leave you vulnerable!</string>
    <string>On higher difficulties, taking damage will interrupt an attack. Hit them before they hit you!</string>
    <string>Weapons and shields can break. Keep an eye on the bar below their inventory icon.</string>
    <string>Smaller shields offer less protection. Try to angle your block into incoming attacks.</string>
    <string>Place traps like Bearjaws and then lure enemies into them.</string>
    <string>Pick up boulders to crush your enemies!</string>
    <string>Visit the Market to buy better weapons, armour, and crafting recipes.</string>
    <string>Some enemies carry trumpets, and can call for reinforcements!</string>
    <string>Some weapons, like spears, have a long reach. Keep enemies from getting too close!</string>
    <string>Switch difficulty at any time in the Options menu.</string>
    <string>Use enhancement potions like the Elixir of Vigor to give yourself an edge in a difficult fight.</string>
    <string>Low on supplies? Retreat to the Market and restock!</string>
    <string>Break crates and jars to find useful items inside.</string>
    <string>Don't let guards catch you vandalizing Olympian property, or be prepared to pay the price!</string>
    <string>Purchase weapon training in the Market for better damage and higher attack-speeds.</string>
    <string>Once discovered, rare weapons will appear in the Black Market shop, and in Lockboxes.</string>
    <string>View your keys and notes in the Inventory menu for clues to hidden treasure!</string>
    <string>Use momentum to add more damage to your strikes! Try jumping and attacking as you fall.</string>
  </Tips>

  <KeyboardTips>
    <string>Dodge attacks and projectiles by rolling (Roll).</string>
    <string>Roll (Roll) past shields in combat to get behind enemies.</string>
    <string>Any attack can be cancelled out of by using the shield (Shield).</string>
    <string>Opponents can be pushed by blocking with your shield (Shield).</string>
    <string>You can throw any weapon with (Throw) to catch opponents off guard.</string>
    <string>Look around (Look Around) while aiming to perform long ranged shots.</string>

    <string>Perform an overhead slash by moving the mouse upwards when charging an attack.</string>
    <string>Perform an uppercut slash by moving the mouse downwards when charging an attack.</string>
    <string>Press (Inventory) to view more detailed inventory information.</string>
    <string>Press (Inventory) to change the look of your armour.</string>
    <string>Press (Local Map) to view more detailed map information.</string>
    <string>Press (World Map) to see the entire map of Mount Olympus.</string>
    <string>Press (Craft) to craft useful items, like nectars and traps.</string>
    <string>Use keys to quickly select weapons, (Select Melee) for melee, (Select Projectile) for projectiles, and (Select Bomb/Trap) for bombs and traps.</string>
    <string>Use the inventory menu (Inventory) to pause for a moment to think and re-equip yourself.</string>
    <string>While blocking with a shield, press (Throw) for a quick shield-bash attack.</string>
  </KeyboardTips>

  <PS4Tips>
    <string>Dodge attacks and projectiles by rolling (Circle).</string>
    <string>Roll (Circle) past shields in combat to get behind enemies.</string>
    <string>Any attack can be cancelled out of by using the shield (L2).</string>
    <string>Opponents can be pushed by blocking with your shield (L2).</string>
    <string>You can throw any weapon with (R1) to catch opponents off guard.</string>
    <string>Look around (Press right stick) while aiming to perform long ranged shots.</string>

    <string>Use the inventory menu to change the look of your armour.</string>
    <string>Perform an overhead slash by moving the left stick upwards when charging an attack.</string>
    <string>Perform an uppercut slash by moving the left stick downwards when charging an attack.</string>
    <string>Use the inventory menu to pause for a moment to think and re-equip yourself.</string>
    <string>While blocking with a shield, press (R1) for a quick shield-bash attack.</string>
  </PS4Tips>

  <GamepadTips>
    <string>Dodge attacks and projectiles by rolling (Roll).</string>
    <string>Roll (Roll) past shields in combat to get behind enemies.</string>
    <string>Any attack can be cancelled out of by using the shield (Shield).</string>
    <string>Opponents can be pushed by blocking with your shield (Shield).</string>
    <string>You can throw any weapon with (Throw) to catch opponents off guard.</string>
    <string>Look around (Look Around) while aiming to perform long ranged shots.</string>

    <string>Use the inventory menu to change the look of your armour.</string>
    <string>Perform an overhead slash by moving the left stick upwards when charging an attack.</string>
    <string>Perform an uppercut slash by moving the left stick downwards when charging an attack.</string>
    <string>Use the inventory menu to pause for a moment to think and re-equip yourself.</string>
    <string>While blocking with a shield, press (Throw) for a quick shield-bash attack.</string>
  </GamepadTips>
  
